  "steps": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. "
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Arrange the poblanos, bell pepper, and jalapeños on a baking sheet. Roast for 20–25 minutes, turning halfway through, until softened and blistered."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Let peppers cool until safe to handle. Remove stems and seeds. Peel away loose, charred skin from the poblanos and bell pepper if desired."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "If using oil, heat it in a saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 5–8 minutes, stirring until softened and excess moisture has evaporated. Add the frozen minced garlic and cook for another 1–2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Transfer the roasted peppers and cooked aromatics to a blender. Add the vinegar, lime juice, salt, cumin, and ¼ cup water. Blend until smooth, adding more water as needed."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Return the sauce to the saucepan. Bring to a gentle simmer for 5–10 minutes, stirring occasionally."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Taste and adjust the salt and acidity. For a thinner, smoother sauce, press it through a fine-mesh strainer."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Transfer to a clean container and refrigerate promptly, or freeze in small portions once cooled."
    }
  ],
